From ac6f8e665438dba9862c43afa492fe155ef4dfca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:48:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] port 16c85fc4: conversation cache: the physical-RAM gates
 stop evicting when the memory does not come back, and a slot's capture can
 evict to fit (opt-in STRATA_GATE_EVICT=1, #3115)

The park admission gate evicts the least recently active parked conversations until the guard's reading admits
the snapshot.  With plain malloc glibc keeps what an eviction frees in its arenas, the reading does not rise, and
the loop emptied the whole cache and refused anyway (measured on the production host).  Against an unknown
reading (which never admits) it did the same.

STRATA_GATE_EVICT=1 (default off; off is the gate exactly as before) runs the park gate through
gate_evict_to_fit (conversation_memory.hpp, pure, header-only):
* no eviction at all when every evictable entry, all of it returned, could not cover allocation + floor, or
  when the reading is unknown; the same check after each eviction against the rest;
* one entry at a time, oldest first (evict_oldest, as before), and a stop after 2 evictions in a row that each
  did not raise the reading by at least half of the entry's accounted bytes (a returning one resets the count).
One new line says why it stopped ("STRATA_GATE_EVICT: stopped evicting after N (...)"); the existing refusal and
"evicted N parked conversations" lines keep their format.

ConversationCache::evictable_bytes() / oldest_evictable_bytes(): the bytes of the entries evict_oldest() may
take and of the next victim.  Tests: conversation_memory_test (stop rule, can-help, returned, saturation,
unknown, bounds), conversation_cache_test (pinned entries are not counted).

Adaptations to v0.2.12:
- Park-gate half only.  The slot-capture half (slot_park_start evicting to fit the RAM floor) needs
  STRATA_SLOT_PARK, which v0.2.12 does not have; it follows with that port.  The env comment and the startup
  line no longer mention the slot capture.
- evictable_bytes() / oldest_evictable_bytes() also leave out upstream's guard()ed borrow donor (#1164), which
  upstream's evict_oldest() skips; a conversation_cache_test case checks it.  No EvictSink / <functional>
  (that belongs to STRATA_CONV_TIER_DIR, a later group).
- The park gate (inside upstream's park_source, shared by park_current and park_slot) re-placed by function;
  gate_evict_env() sits after the slot_copy_batchsync switch (our base had it beside slot_park_env).
- conversation_memory_test: our cases appended after upstream's auto_conversation_cache_mib checks.

(cherry picked from commit 16c85fc4d99059cfbb77470929d294c253daccb3)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
